    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d592">

                <pb facs="0652" n="540" xml:id="pg540"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/5508: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Tenney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-28"><hi rendition="#italic">October 28,
                        1919</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received October 29, 10:10 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>[From Harris at Omsk:]</p>
                <p>448. October 28th, 5 p.m.</p>
                <p>Referring to Department’s two telegrams dated October 25th, 5 p.m., and October
                    25th, 6 p.m.<anchor n="86" xml:id="d592-f1"/> Soukine informs me that this
                    matter will be taken before the Council of Ministers and he believes it will
                    receive favorable decision.</p>
                <p>I can confirm Smith’s viewpoint that there
                    is an improvement already in the attitude of the Russians, especially
                        Ustrugoff, who is becoming very conciliatory.</p>
                <p>Respectfully urge upon the Department advisability of requesting Stevens not to withdraw railway inspectors just
                    at this time. Harris.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Tenney</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
